      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "What you're asking for is basically a more dynamic rating system, this could in theory be achieved if the average performance of maxed out avatars is taken as a \"control\" reference, and if you save on resources somewhere and gain sufficient (theoretical) performance headroom you'd gain more slots for other types of resources to remain as \"green\", this would be a nice-to-have but I doubt the priority on a system like this.\n\nAlternatively they could just increase the component count they allow but at that point it no longer \"makes up\" for you using 32 transforms.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
